      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 554: 🔴 `pj_sock_setsockopt()` takes `optlen` as `pj_size_t` and forwards it to `setsockopt()`. On Windows the native `setsockopt()` expects an `int` length, so passing `sizeof(val)` directly can fail to compile because `pj_size_t` is `size_t`. Use the existing pjlib Windows pattern with a local `int optlen \u003d sizeof(val)` or adjust the helper so the Windows call receives the expected length type.",
      "revId": "406e1f430d5407d0c4c675d0862f6d46cdffcb9e",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
